          "text": "{\"snapshotId\":\"capture-9aba1d48-0f49-4951-9829-4c6a964a4fe8\",\"url\":\"https://react.dev/blog/2024/04/25/react-19-upgrade-guide\",\"title\":\"React 19 Upgrade Guide – React\",\"capturedAt\":\"2026-10-10T03:08:19.584Z\",\"text\":\"[characters 293-486]\\nTo help make the upgrade to React 19 easier, we’ve published a react@18.3 release that is identical to 18.2 but adds warnings for deprecated APIs and other changes that are needed for React 19.\\n\\n[characters 1069-1304]\\nWe introduced a new JSX transform in 2020 to improve bundle size and use JSX without importing React. In React 19, we’re adding additional improvements like using ref as a prop and JSX speed improvements that require the new transform.\\n\\n[characters 2966-3072]\\nreplace-reactdom-render\\nreplace-string-ref\\nreplace-act-import\\nreplace-use-form-state\\nprop-types-typescript\\n\\n[characters 4299-4380]\\nRemoved deprecated React APIs \\nRemoved: propTypes and defaultProps for functions \\n\\n[characters 4382-4432]\\nPropTypes were deprecated in April 2017 (v15.5.0).\\n\\n[characters 4647-4830]\\nWe’re also removing defaultProps from function components in place of ES6 default parameters. Class components will continue to support defaultProps since there is no ES6 alternative.\\n\\n[characters 5226-5336]\\nnpx codemod@latest react/prop-types-typescript\\nRemoved: Legacy Context using contextTypes and getChildContext \\n\\n[characters 5338-5394]\\nLegacy Context was deprecated in October 2018 (v16.6.0).\\n\\n[characters 5396-5661]\\nLegacy Context was only available in class components using the APIs contextTypes and getChildContext, and was replaced with contextType due to subtle bugs that were easy to miss. In React 19, we’re removing Legacy Context to make React slightly smaller and faster.\\n\\n[characters 5663-5771]\\nIf you’re still using Legacy Context in class components, you’ll need to migrate to the new contextType API:\\n\\n[characters 5823-5861]\\nclass Parent extends React.Component {\\n\\n[characters 6047-6084]\\nclass Child extends React.Component {\\n\\n[characters 6279-6317]\\nclass Parent extends React.Component {\\n\\n[characters 6437-6474]\\nclass Child extends React.Component {\\n\\n[characters 6572-6595]\\n}\\nRemoved: string refs \\n\\n[characters 6597-6650]\\nString refs were deprecated in March, 2018 (v16.3.0).\\n\\n[characters 6652-6844]\\nClass components supported string refs before being replaced by ref callbacks due to multiple downsides. In React 19, we’re removing string refs to make React simpler and easier to understand.\\n\\n[characters 6846-6941]\\nIf you’re still using string refs in class components, you’ll need to migrate to ref callbacks:\\n\\n[characters 6954-6997]\\nclass MyComponent extends React.Component {\\n\\n[characters 7024-7052]\\n    this.refs.input.focus();\\n\\n[characters 7075-7108]\\n    return <input ref='input' />;\\n\\n[characters 7127-7170]\\nclass MyComponent extends React.Component {\\n\\n[characters 7243-7298]\\n    return <input ref={input => this.input = input} />;\\n\\n[characters 7313-7352]\\nCodemod string refs with ref callbacks:\\n\\n[characters 7354-7435]\\nnpx codemod@latest react/19/replace-string-ref\\nRemoved: Module pattern factories \\n\\n[characters 7437-7503]\\nModule pattern factories were deprecated in August 2019 (v16.9.0).\\n\\n[characters 7877-7908]\\n}\\nRemoved: React.createFactory \\n\\n[characters 7910-7967]\\ncreateFactory was deprecated in February 2020 (v16.13.0).\\n\\n[characters 8268-8332]\\nconst button = <button />;\\nRemoved: react-test-renderer/shallow \\n\\n[characters 8334-8519]\\nIn React 18, we updated react-test-renderer/shallow to re-export react-shallow-renderer. In React 19, we’re removing react-test-render/shallow to prefer installing the package directly:\\n\\n[characters 8908-8973]\\nRemoved deprecated React DOM APIs \\nRemoved: react-dom/test-utils \\n\\n[characters 9040-9228]\\nConsole\\nReactDOMTestUtils.act is deprecated in favor of React.act. Import act from react instead of react-dom/test-utils. See https://react.dev/warnings/react-dom-test-utils for more info.\\n\\n[characters 9357-9641]\\nAll other test-utils functions have been removed. These utilities were uncommon, and made it too easy to depend on low level implementation details of your components and React. In React 19, these functions will error when called and their exports will be removed in a future version.\\n\\n[characters 9734-9806]\\nnpx codemod@latest react/19/replace-act-import\\nRemoved: ReactDOM.render \\n\\n[characters 9808-9964]\\nReactDOM.render was deprecated in March 2022 (v18.0.0). In React 19, we’re removing ReactDOM.render and you’ll need to migrate to using ReactDOM.createRoot:\\n\\n[characters 10263-10341]\\nnpx codemod@latest react/19/replace-reactdom-render\\nRemoved: ReactDOM.hydrate \\n\\n[characters 10343-10498]\\nReactDOM.hydrate was deprecated in March 2022 (v18.0.0). In React 19, we’re removing ReactDOM.hydrate you’ll need to migrate to using ReactDOM.hydrateRoot,\\n\\n[characters 10776-10860]\\nnpx codemod@latest react/19/replace-reactdom-render\\nRemoved: unmountComponentAtNode \\n\\n[characters 10862-10994]\\nReactDOM.unmountComponentAtNode was deprecated in March 2022 (v18.0.0). In React 19, you’ll need to migrate to using root.unmount().\\n\\n[characters 11210-11292]\\nnpx codemod@latest react/19/replace-reactdom-render\\nRemoved: ReactDOM.findDOMNode \\n\\n[characters 11294-11356]\\nReactDOM.findDOMNode was deprecated in October 2018 (v16.6.0).\\n\\n[characters 11358-11471]\\nWe’re removing findDOMNode because it was a legacy escape hatch that was slow to execute, fragile to refactoring,\",\"truncated\":true,\"query\":\"forwardRef ref cleanups deprecated removed class components\",\"excerpts\":[{\"charStart\":293,\"charEnd\":486,\"text\":\"To help make the upgrade to React 19 easier, we’ve published a react@18.3 release that is identical to 18.2 but adds warnings for deprecated APIs and other changes that are needed for React 19.\"},{\"charStart\":1069,\"charEnd\":1304,\"text\":\"We introduced a new JSX transform in 2020 to improve bundle size and use JSX without importing React. In React 19, we’re adding additional improvements like using ref as a prop and JSX speed improvements that require the new transform.\"},{\"charStart\":2966,\"charEnd\":3072,\"text\":\"replace-reactdom-render\\nreplace-string-ref\\nreplace-act-import\\nreplace-use-form-state\\nprop-types-typescript\"},{\"charStart\":4299,\"charEnd\":4380,\"text\":\"Removed deprecated React APIs \\nRemoved: propTypes and defaultProps for functions \"},{\"charStart\":4382,\"charEnd\":4432,\"text\":\"PropTypes were deprecated in April 2017 (v15.5.0).\"},{\"charStart\":4647,\"charEnd\":4830,\"text\":\"We’re also removing defaultProps from function components in place of ES6 default parameters. Class components will continue to support defaultProps since there is no ES6 alternative.\"},{\"charStart\":5226,\"charEnd\":5336,\"text\":\"npx codemod@latest react/prop-types-typescript\\nRemoved: Legacy Context using contextTypes and getChildContext \"},{\"charStart\":5338,\"charEnd\":5394,\"text\":\"Legacy Context was deprecated in October 2018 (v16.6.0).\"},{\"charStart\":5396,\"charEnd\":5661,\"text\":\"Legacy Context was only available in class components using the APIs contextTypes and getChildContext, and was replaced with contextType due to subtle bugs that were easy to miss. In React 19, we’re removing Legacy Context to make React slightly smaller and faster.\"},{\"charStart\":5663,\"charEnd\":5771,\"text\":\"If you’re still using Legacy Context in class components, you’ll need to migrate to the new contextType API:\"},{\"charStart\":5823,\"charEnd\":5861,\"text\":\"class Parent extends React.Component {\"},{\"charStart\":6047,\"charEnd\":6084,\"text\":\"class Child extends React.Component {\"},{\"charStart\":6279,\"charEnd\":6317,\"text\":\"class Parent extends React.Component {\"},{\"charStart\":