          "type": "text",
          "text": "{\"snapshotId\":\"capture-9aba1d48-0f49-4951-9829-4c6a964a4fe8\",\"url\":\"https://react.dev/blog/2024/04/25/react-19-upgrade-guide\",\"title\":\"React 19 Upgrade Guide – React\",\"capturedAt\":\"2026-10-10T03:08:19.584Z\",\"text\":\"[characters 293-486]\\nTo help make the upgrade to React 19 easier, we’ve published a react@18.3 release that is identical to 18.2 but adds warnings for deprecated APIs and other changes that are needed for React 19.\\n\\n[characters 1016-1067]\\nInstalling \\nNote\\nNew JSX Transform is now required \\n\\n[characters 1069-1304]\\nWe introduced a new JSX transform in 2020 to improve bundle size and use JSX without importing React. In React 19, we’re adding additional improvements like using ref as a prop and JSX speed improvements that require the new transform.\\n\\n[characters 2966-3072]\\nreplace-reactdom-render\\nreplace-string-ref\\nreplace-act-import\\nreplace-use-form-state\\nprop-types-typescript\\n\\n[characters 4299-4380]\\nRemoved deprecated React APIs \\nRemoved: propTypes and defaultProps for functions \\n\\n[characters 4382-4432]\\nPropTypes were deprecated in April 2017 (v15.5.0).\\n\\n[characters 5338-5394]\\nLegacy Context was deprecated in October 2018 (v16.6.0).\\n\\n[characters 5895-5932]\\n    foo: PropTypes.string.isRequired,\\n\\n[characters 6113-6150]\\n    foo: PropTypes.string.isRequired,\\n\\n[characters 6572-6595]\\n}\\nRemoved: string refs \\n\\n[characters 6597-6650]\\nString refs were deprecated in March, 2018 (v16.3.0).\\n\\n[characters 6652-6844]\\nClass components supported string refs before being replaced by ref callbacks due to multiple downsides. In React 19, we’re removing string refs to make React simpler and easier to understand.\\n\\n[characters 6846-6941]\\nIf you’re still using string refs in class components, you’ll need to migrate to ref callbacks:\\n\\n[characters 7024-7052]\\n    this.refs.input.focus();\\n\\n[characters 7075-7108]\\n    return <input ref='input' />;\\n\\n[characters 7243-7298]\\n    return <input ref={input => this.input = input} />;\\n\\n[characters 7313-7352]\\nCodemod string refs with ref callbacks:\\n\\n[characters 7354-7435]\\nnpx codemod@latest react/19/replace-string-ref\\nRemoved: Module pattern factories \\n\\n[characters 7437-7503]\\nModule pattern factories were deprecated in August 2019 (v16.9.0).\\n\\n[characters 7910-7967]\\ncreateFactory was deprecated in February 2020 (v16.13.0).\\n\\n[characters 8334-8519]\\nIn React 18, we updated react-test-renderer/shallow to re-export react-shallow-renderer. In React 19, we’re removing react-test-render/shallow to prefer installing the package directly:\\n\\n[characters 8908-8973]\\nRemoved deprecated React DOM APIs \\nRemoved: react-dom/test-utils \\n\\n[characters 9040-9228]\\nConsole\\nReactDOMTestUtils.act is deprecated in favor of React.act. Import act from react instead of react-dom/test-utils. See https://react.dev/warnings/react-dom-test-utils for more info.\\n\\n[characters 9808-9964]\\nReactDOM.render was deprecated in March 2022 (v18.0.0). In React 19, we’re removing ReactDOM.render and you’ll need to migrate to using ReactDOM.createRoot:\\n\\n[characters 10343-10498]\\nReactDOM.hydrate was deprecated in March 2022 (v18.0.0). In React 19, we’re removing ReactDOM.hydrate you’ll need to migrate to using ReactDOM.hydrateRoot,\\n\\n[characters 10862-10994]\\nReactDOM.unmountComponentAtNode was deprecated in March 2022 (v18.0.0). In React 19, you’ll need to migrate to using root.unmount().\\n\\n[characters 11294-11356]\\nReactDOM.findDOMNode was deprecated in October 2018 (v16.6.0).\\n\\n[characters 11358-11600]\\nWe’re removing findDOMNode because it was a legacy escape hatch that was slow to execute, fragile to refactoring, only returned the first child, and broke abstraction levels (see more here). You can replace ReactDOM.findDOMNode with DOM refs:\\n\\n[characters 11867-11894]\\n  const ref = useRef(null);\\n\\n[characters 11917-11942]\\n    ref.current.select();\\n\\n[characters 11957-12006]\\n  return <input ref={ref} defaultValue=\\\"Hello\\\" />\\n\\n[characters 12008-12052]\\n}\\nNew deprecations \\nDeprecated: element.ref \\n\\n[characters 12054-12154]\\nReact 19 supports ref as a prop, so we’re deprecating the element.ref in place of element.props.ref.\\n\\n[characters 12156-12188]\\nAccessing element.ref will warn:\\n\\n[characters 12190-12369]\\nConsole\\nAccessing element.ref is no longer supported. ref is now a regular prop. It will be removed from the JSX Element type in a future release.\\nDeprecated: react-test-renderer \\n\\n[characters 13384-13762]\\nAs with all Strict Mode behaviors, these features are designed to proactively surface bugs in your components during development so you can fix them before they are shipped to production. For example, during development, Strict Mode will double-invoke ref callback functions on initial mount, to simulate what happens when a mounted component is replaced by a Suspense fallback.\\n\\n[characters 15573-15662]\\nTo reflect the impact of using internals, we have renamed the SECRET_INTERNALS suffix to:\\n\\n[characters 15858-15914]\\nTypeScript changes \\nRemoved deprecated TypeScript types \\n\\n[characters 16620-16642]\\nref cleanups required \\n\\n[characters 16644-16735]\\nThis change is included in the react-19 codemod preset as no-implicit-ref-callback-return .\\n\\n[characters 16737-16917]\\nDue to the introduction of ref cleanup functions, returning anything else from a ref callback will now be rejected by TypeScript. The fix is usually to stop using implicit returns:\\n\\n[characters 16919-16966]\\n- <div ref={current => (instance = current)} />\\n\\n[characters 16968-16992]\\n+ <div ref={current => {\",\"truncated\":true,\"query\":\"forwardRef deprecated ref cleanups required\",\"excerpts\":[{\"charStart\":293,\"charEnd\":486,\"text\":\"To help make the upgrade to React 19 easier, we’ve published a react@18.3 release that is identical to 18.2 but adds warnings for deprecated APIs and other changes that are needed for React 19.\"},{\"charStart\":1016,\"charEnd\":1067,\"text\":\"Installing \\nNote\\nNew JSX Transform is now required \"},{\"charStart\":1069,\"charEnd\":1304,\"text\":\"We introduced a new JSX transform in 2020 to improve bundle size and use JSX without importing React. In React 19, we’re adding additional improvements like using ref as a prop and JSX speed improvements that require the new transform.\"},{\"charStart\":2966,\"charEnd\":3072,\"text\":\"replace-reactdom-render\\nreplace-string-ref\\nreplace-act-import\\nreplace-use-form-state\\nprop-types-typescript\"},{\"charStart\":4299,\"charEnd\":4380,\"text\":\"Removed deprecated React APIs \\nRemoved: propTypes and defaultProps for functions \"},{\"charStart\":4382,\"charEnd\":4432,\"text\":\"PropTypes were deprecated in April 2017 (v15.5.0).\"},{\"charStart\":5338,\"charEnd\":5394,\"text\":\"Legacy Context was deprecated in October 2018 (v16.6.0).\"},{\"charStart\":5895,\"charEnd\":5932,\"text\":\"    foo: PropTypes.string.isRequired,\"},{\"charStart\":6113,\"charEnd\":6150,\"text\":\"    foo: PropTypes.string.isRequired,\"},{\"charStart\":6572,\"charEnd\":6595,\"text\":\"}\\nRemoved: string refs \"},{\"charStart\":6597,\"charEnd\":6650,\"text\":\"String refs were deprecated in March, 2018 (v16.3.0).\"},{\"charStart\":6652,\"charEnd\":6844,\"text\":\"Class components supported string refs before being replaced by ref callbacks due to multiple downsides. In React 19, we’re removing string refs to make React simpler and easier to understand.\"},{\"charStart\":6846,\"charEnd\":6941,\"text\":\"If you’re still using string refs in class components, you’ll need to migrate to ref callbacks:\"},{\"charStart\":7024,\"charEnd\":7052,\"text\":\"    this.refs.input.focus();\"},{\"charStart\":7075,\"charEnd\":7108,\"text\":\"    return <input ref='input' />;\"},{\"charStart\":7243,\"charEnd\":7298,\"text\":\"    return <input ref={input => this.input = input} />;\"},{\"charStart\":7313,\"charEnd\":7352,\"text\":\"Codemod string refs with ref callbacks:\"},{\"charStart\":7354,\"charEnd\":7435,\"text\":\"npx codemod@latest react/19/replace-string-ref\\nRemoved: Module pattern factories \"},{\"charStart\":7437,\"charEnd\":7503,\"text\":\"Module pattern factories were deprecated in August 2019 (v16.9.0).\"},{\"charStart\":7910,\"charEnd\":7967,\"text\":\"createFactory was deprecated in February 2020 (v16.13.0).\"},{\"charStart\":8334,\"charEnd\":8519,\"text\":\"In React 18, we updated react-test-renderer/shallow to re-export react-shallow-renderer. In React 19, we’re removing react-test-render/shallow to prefer installing the package directly:\"},{\"charStart\":8908,\"charEnd\":8973,\"text\":\"Removed deprecated React DOM APIs \\nRemoved: react-dom/test-utils \"},{\"charStart\":9040,\"charEnd\":9228,\"text\":\"Console\\nReactDOMTestUtils.act is deprecated in favor of React.act. Import act from react instead of react-dom/test-utils. See https://react.dev/warnings/react-dom-test-utils for more info.\"},{\"charStart\":9808,\"charEnd\":9964,\"text\":\"ReactDOM.render was deprecated in March 2022 (v18.0.0). In React 19, we’re removing ReactDOM.render and you’ll need to migrate to using ReactDOM.createRoot:\"},{\"charStart\":10343,\"charEnd\":10498,\"text\":\"ReactDOM.hydrate was deprecated in March 2022 (v18.0.0). In React 19, we’re removing ReactDOM.hydrate you’ll need to migrate to using ReactDOM.hydrateRoot,\"},{\"charStart\":10862,\"charEnd\":10994,\"text\":\"ReactDOM.unmountComponentAtNode was deprecated in March 2022 (v18.0.0). In React 19, you’ll need to migrate to using root.unmount().\"},{\"charStart\":11294,\"charEnd\":11356,\"text\":\"ReactDOM.findDOMNode was deprecated in October 2018 (v16.6.0).\"},{\"charStart\":11358,\"charEnd\":11600,\"text\":\"We’re removing findDOMNode because it was a legacy escape hatch that was slow to execute, fragile to refactoring, only returned the first child, and broke abstraction levels (see more here). You can replace ReactDOM.findDOMNode with DOM refs:\"},{\"charStart\":11867,\"charEnd\":11894,\"text\":\"  const ref = useRef(null);\"},{\"charStart\":11917,\"charEnd\":11942,\"text\":\"    ref.current.select();\"},{\"charStart\":11957,\"charEnd\":12006,\"text\":\"  return <input ref={ref} defaultValue=\\\"Hello\\\" />\"},{\"charStart\":12008,\"charEnd\":12052,\"text\":\"}\\nNew deprecations \\nDeprecated: element.ref \"},{\"charStart\":12054,\"charEnd\":12154,\"text\":\"React 19 supports ref as a prop, so we’re deprecating the element.ref in place of element.props.ref.\"},{\"charStart\":12156,\"charEnd\":12188,\"text\":\"Accessing element.ref will warn:\"},{\"charStart\":12190,\"charEnd\":12369,\"text\":\"Console\\nAccessing element.ref is no longer supported. ref is now a regular prop. It will be removed from the JSX Element type in a future release.\\nDeprecated: react-test-renderer \"},{\"charStart\":13384,\"charEnd\":13762,\"text\":\"As with all Strict Mode behaviors, these features are designed to proactively surface bugs in your components during development so you can fix them before they are shipped to production. For example, during development, Strict Mode will double-invoke ref callback functions on initial mount, to simulate what happens when a mounted component is replaced by a Suspense fallback.\"},{\"charStart\":15573,\"charEnd\":15662,\"text\":\"To reflect the impact of using internals, we have renamed the SECRET_INTERNALS suffix to:\"},{\"charStart\":15858,\"charEnd\":15914,\"text\":\"TypeScript changes \\nRemoved deprecated TypeScript types \"},{\"charStart\":16620,\"charEnd\":16642,\"text\":\"ref cleanups required \"},{\"charStart\":16644,\"charEnd\":16735,\"text\":\"This change is included in the react-19 codemod preset as no-implicit-ref-callback-return .\"},{\"charStart\":16737,\"charEnd\":16917,\"text\":\"Due to the introduction of ref cleanup functions, returning anything else from a ref callback will now be rejected by TypeScript. The fix is usually to stop using implicit returns:\"},{\"charStart\":16919,\"charEnd\":16966,\"text\":\"- <div ref={current => (instance = current)} />\"},{\"charStart\":16968,\"charEnd\":16992,\"text\":\"+ <div ref={current => {\"}],\"sourcePath\":\"C:\\\\Temp\\\\weftmate-fact1-d4639fa5-93d3-4c19-b0c5-3adfc5860d9e\\\\profile\\\\conversations\\\\aece5e58c4cf64f78c9e3bccc03bda00a1c56ee594e7081cc97810825cad01da\\\\session-3a0d1e90-b75c-49be-8062-fba6e990a659\\\\.weftmate-web-sources\\\\capture-9aba1d48-0f49-4951-9829-4c6a964a4fe8.txt\"}"
