          "type": "text",
          "text": "{\"snapshotId\":\"capture-9aba1d48-0f49-4951-9829-4c6a964a4fe8\",\"url\":\"https://react.dev/blog/2024/04/25/react-19-upgrade-guide\",\"title\":\"React 19 Upgrade Guide – React\",\"capturedAt\":\"2026-10-10T03:08:19.584Z\",\"text\":\"[characters 0-37]\\nBLOG\\nCopy page\\nReact 19 Upgrade Guide\\n\\n[characters 39-69]\\nApril 25, 2024 by Ricky Hanlon\\n\\n[characters 71-249]\\nThe improvements added to React 19 require some breaking changes, but we’ve worked to make the upgrade as smooth as possible, and we don’t expect the changes to impact most apps.\\n\\n[characters 251-291]\\nNote\\nReact 18.3 has also been published \\n\\n[characters 293-486]\\nTo help make the upgrade to React 19 easier, we’ve published a react@18.3 release that is identical to 18.2 but adds warnings for deprecated APIs and other changes that are needed for React 19.\\n\\n[characters 488-588]\\nWe recommend upgrading to React 18.3 first to help identify any issues before upgrading to React 19.\\n\\n[characters 590-642]\\nFor a list of changes in 18.3 see the Release Notes.\\n\\n[characters 644-720]\\nIn this post, we will guide you through the steps for upgrading to React 19:\\n\\n[characters 722-820]\\nInstalling\\nCodemods\\nBreaking changes\\nNew deprecations\\nNotable changes\\nTypeScript changes\\nChangelog\\n\\n[characters 822-1014]\\nIf you’d like to help us test React 19, follow the steps in this upgrade guide and report any issues you encounter. For a list of new features added to React 19, see the React 19 release post.\\n\\n[characters 1016-1067]\\nInstalling \\nNote\\nNew JSX Transform is now required \\n\\n[characters 1069-1304]\\nWe introduced a new JSX transform in 2020 to improve bundle size and use JSX without importing React. In React 19, we’re adding additional improvements like using ref as a prop and JSX speed improvements that require the new transform.\\n\\n[characters 1306-1369]\\nIf the new transform is not enabled, you will see this warning:\\n\\n[characters 1371-1552]\\nConsole\\nYour app (or one of its dependencies) is using an outdated JSX transform. Update to the modern JSX transform for faster performance: https://react.dev/link/new-jsx-transform\\n\\n[characters 1554-1732]\\nWe expect most apps will not be affected since the transform is enabled in most environments already. For manual instructions on how to upgrade, please see the announcement post.\\n\\n[characters 1734-1787]\\nTo install the latest version of React and React DOM:\\n\\n[characters 1789-1845]\\nnpm install --save-exact react@^19.0.0 react-dom@^19.0.0\\n\\n[characters 1847-1872]\\nOr, if you’re using Yarn:\\n\\n[characters 1874-1922]\\nyarn add --exact react@^19.0.0 react-dom@^19.0.0\\n\\n[characters 1924-1986]\\nIf you’re using TypeScript, you also need to update the types.\\n\\n[characters 1988-2058]\\nnpm install --save-exact @types/react@^19.0.0 @types/react-dom@^19.0.0\\n\\n[characters 2060-2085]\\nOr, if you’re using Yarn:\\n\\n[characters 2087-2149]\\nyarn add --exact @types/react@^19.0.0 @types/react-dom@^19.0.0\\n\\n[characters 2151-2245]\\nWe’re also including a codemod for the most common replacements. See TypeScript changes below.\\n\\n[characters 2258-2436]\\nTo help with the upgrade, we’ve worked with the team at codemod.com to publish codemods that will automatically update your code to many of the new APIs and patterns in React 19.\\n\\n[characters 2438-2754]\\nAll codemods are available in the react-codemod repo and the Codemod team have joined in helping maintain the codemods. To run these codemods, we recommend using the codemod command instead of the react-codemod because it runs faster, handles more complex code migrations, and provides better support for TypeScript.\\n\\n[characters 2756-2787]\\nNote\\nRun all React 19 codemods \\n\\n[characters 2789-2860]\\nRun all codemods listed in this guide with the React 19 codemod recipe:\\n\\n[characters 2862-2906]\\nnpx codemod@latest react/19/migration-recipe\\n\\n[characters 2908-2964]\\nThis will run the following codemods from react-codemod:\\n\\n[characters 2966-3072]\\nreplace-reactdom-render\\nreplace-string-ref\\nreplace-act-import\\nreplace-use-form-state\\nprop-types-typescript\\n\\n[characters 3074-3149]\\nThis does not include the TypeScript changes. See TypeScript changes below.\\n\\n[characters 3151-3208]\\nChanges that include a codemod include the command below.\\n\\n[characters 3210-3275]\\nFor a list of all available codemods, see the react-codemod repo.\\n\\n[characters 3277-3330]\\nBreaking changes \\nErrors in render are not re-thrown \\n\\n[characters 3332-3495]\\nIn previous versions of React, errors thrown during render were caught and rethrown. In DEV, we would also log to console.error, resulting in duplicate error logs.\\n\\n[characters 3497-3589]\\nIn React 19, we’ve improved how errors are handled to reduce duplication by not re-throwing:\\n\\n[characters 3591-3781]\\nUncaught Errors: Errors that are not caught by an Error Boundary are reported to window.reportError.\\nCaught Errors: Errors that are caught by an Error Boundary are reported to console.error.\\n\\n[characters 3783-4038]\\nThis change should not impact most apps, but if your production error reporting relies on errors being re-thrown, you may need to update your error handling. To support this, we’ve added new methods to createRoot and hydrateRoot for custom error handling:\\n\\n[characters 4040-4076]\\nconst root = createRoot(container, {\\n\\n[characters 4078-4120]\\n  onUncaughtError: (error, errorInfo) => {\\n\\n[characters 4157-4197]\\n  onCaughtError: (error, errorInfo) => {\\n\\n[characters 4238-4265]\\nFor more info, see the docs\",\"truncated\":true,\"query\":\"element.ref deprecated ref as a prop TypeScript changes\",\"excerpts\":[{\"charStart\":0,\"charEnd\":37,\"text\":\"BLOG\\nCopy page\\nReact 19 Upgrade Guide\"},{\"charStart\":39,\"charEnd\":69,\"text\":\"April 25, 2024 by Ricky Hanlon\"},{\"charStart\":71,\"charEnd\":249,\"text\":\"The improvements added to React 19 require some breaking changes, but we’ve worked to make the upgrade as smooth as possible, and we don’t expect the changes to impact most apps.\"},{\"charStart\":251,\"charEnd\":291,\"text\":\"Note\\nReact 18.3 has also been published \"},{\"charStart\":293,\"charEnd\":486,\"text\":\"To help make the upgrade to React 19 easier, we’ve published a react@18.3 release that is identical to 18.2 but adds warnings for deprecated APIs and other changes that are needed for React 19.\"},{\"charStart\":488,\"charEnd\":588,\"text\":\"We recommend upgrading to React 18.3 first to help identify any issues before upgrading to React 19.\"},{\"charStart\":590,\"charEnd\":642,\"text\":\"For a list of changes in 18.3 see the Release Notes.\"},{\"charStart\":644,\"charEnd\":720,\"text\":\"In this post, we will guide you through the steps for upgrading to React 19:\"},{\"charStart\":722,\"charEnd\":820,\"text\":\"Installing\\nCodemods\\nBreaking changes\\nNew deprecations\\nNotable changes\\nTypeScript changes\\nChangelog\"},{\"charStart\":822,\"charEnd\":1014,\"text\":\"If you’d like to help us test React 19, follow the steps in this upgrade guide and report any issues you encounter. For a list of new features added to React 19, see the React 19 release post.\"},{\"charStart\":1016,\"charEnd\":1067,\"text\":\"Installing \\nNote\\nNew JSX Transform is now required \"},{\"charStart\":1069,\"charEnd\":1304,\"text\":\"We introduced a new JSX transform in 2020 to improve bundle size and use JSX without importing React. In React 19, we’re adding additional improvements like using ref as a prop and JSX speed improvements that require the new transform.\"},{\"charStart\":1306,\"charEnd\":1369,\"text\":\"If the new transform is not enabled, you will see this warning:\"},{\"charStart\":1371,\"charEnd\":1552,\"text\":\"Console\\nYour app (or one of its dependencies) is using an outdated JSX transform. Update to the modern JSX transform for faster performance: https://react.dev/link/new-jsx-transform\"},{\"charStart\":1554,\"charEnd\":1732,\"text\":\"We expect most apps will not be affected since the transform is enabled in most environments already. For manual instructions on how to upgrade, please see the announcement post.\"},{\"charStart\":1734,\"charEnd\":1787,\"text\":\"To install the latest version of React and React DOM:\"},{\"charStart\":1789,\"charEnd\":1845,\"text\":\"npm install --save-exact react@^19.0.0 react-dom@^19.0.0\"},{\"charStart\":1847,\"charEnd\":1872,\"text\":\"Or, if you’re using Yarn:\"},{\"charStart\":1874,\"charEnd\":1922,\"text\":\"yarn add --exact react@^19.0.0 react-dom@^19.0.0\"},{\"charStart\":1924,\"charEnd\":1986,\"text\":\"If you’re using TypeScript, you also need to update the types.\"},{\"charStart\":1988,\"charEnd\":2058,\"text\":\"npm install --save-exact @types/react@^19.0.0 @types/react-dom@^19.0.0\"},{\"charStart\":2060,\"charEnd\":2085,\"text\":\"Or, if you’re using Yarn:\"},{\"charStart\":2087,\"charEnd\":2149,\"text\":\"yarn add --exact @types/react@^19.0.0 @types/react-dom@^19.0.0\"},{\"charStart\":2151,\"charEnd\":2245,\"text\":\"We’re also including a codemod for the most common replacements. See TypeScript changes below.\"},{\"charStart\":2258,\"charEnd\":2436,\"text\":\"To help with the upgrade, we’ve worked with the team at codemod.com to publish codemods that will automatically update your code to many of the new APIs and patterns in React 19.\"},{\"charStart\":2438,\"charEnd\":2754,\"text\":\"All codemods are available in the react-codemod repo and the Codemod team have joined in helping maintain the codemods. To run these codemods, we recommend using the codemod command instead of the react-codemod because it runs faster, handles more complex code migrations, and provides better support for TypeScript.\"},{\"charStart\":2756,\"charEnd\":2787,\"text\":\"Note\\nRun all React 19 codemods \"},{\"charStart\":2789,\"charEnd\":2860,\"text\":\"Run all codemods listed in this guide with the React 19 codemod recipe:\"},{\"charStart\":2862,\"charEnd\":2906,\"text\":\"npx codemod@latest react/19/migration-recipe\"},{\"charStart\":2908,\"charEnd\":2964,\"text\":\"This will run the following codemods from react-codemod:\"},{\"charStart\":2966,\"charEnd\":3072,\"text\":\"replace-reactdom-render\\nreplace-string-ref\\nreplace-act-import\\nreplace-use-form-state\\nprop-types-typescript\"},{\"charStart\":3074,\"charEnd\":3149,\"text\":\"This does not include the TypeScript changes. See TypeScript changes below.\"},{\"charStart\":3151,\"charEnd\":3208,\"text\":\"Changes that include a codemod include the command below.\"},{\"charStart\":3210,\"charEnd\":3275,\"text\":\"For a list of all available codemods, see the react-codemod repo.\"},{\"charStart\":3277,\"charEnd\":3330,\"text\":\"Breaking changes \\nErrors in render are not re-thrown \"},{\"charStart\":3332,\"charEnd\":3495,\"text\":\"In previous versions of React, errors thrown during render were caught and rethrown. In DEV, we would also log to console.error, resulting in duplicate error logs.\"},{\"charStart\":3497,\"charEnd\":3589,\"text\":\"In React 19, we’ve improved how errors are handled to reduce duplication by not re-throwing:\"},{\"charStart\":3591,\"charEnd\":3781,\"text\":\"Uncaught Errors: Errors that are not caught by an Error Boundary are reported to window.reportError.\\nCaught Errors: Errors that are caught by an Error Boundary are reported to console.error.\"},{\"charStart\":3783,\"charEnd\":4038,\"text\":\"This change should not impact most apps, but if your production error reporting relies on errors being re-thrown, you may need to update your error handling. To support this, we’ve added new methods to createRoot and hydrateRoot for custom error handling:\"},{\"charStart\":4040,\"charEnd\":4076,\"text\":\"const root = createRoot(container, {\"},{\"charStart\":4078,\"charEnd\":4120,\"text\":\"  onUncaughtError: (error, errorInfo) => {\"},{\"charStart\":4157,\"charEnd\":4197,\"text\":\"  onCaughtError: (error, errorInfo) => {\"},{\"charStart\":4238,\"charEnd\":4265,\"text\":\"For more info, see the docs\"}],\"sourcePath\":\"C:\\\\Temp\\\\weftmate-fact1-d4639fa5-93d3-4c19-b0c5-3adfc5860d9e\\\\profile\\\\conversations\\\\aece5e58c4cf64f78c9e3bccc03bda00a1c56ee594e7081cc97810825cad01da\\\\session-3a0d1e90-b75c-49be-8062-fba6e990a659\\\\.weftmate-web-sources\\\\capture-9aba1d48-0f49-4951-9829-4c6a964a4fe8.txt\"}"
