nt) and caching ([CACHING]) from the current HTTP/1.1 messaging syntax ([HTTP/1.1]) to allow each major protocol version to progress independently while referring to the same core semantics.\\n\\n[characters 15663-16205]\\nEa\n\n[... tool result middle pruned ...]\n\ns intentions were carried out, determining what to do next based on the status codes and content received.\"},{\"charStart\":16207,\"charEnd\":16507,\"text\":\"HTTP semantics include the intentions defined by each request method (Section 9), extensions to those semantics that might be described in request header fields, status codes that describe the response (Section 15), and other control data and resource metadata that might be given in response fields.\"},{\"charStart\":16509,\"charEnd\":16745,\"text\":\"Semantics also include representation metadata that describe how content is intended to be interpreted by a recipient, request header fields that might influence content selection, and the various selection algorithms that are collectiv\"}],\"sourcePath\":\"C:\\\\Temp\\\\weftmate-fact1-d4639fa5-93d3-4c19-b0c5-3adfc5860d9e\\\\profile\\\\conversations\\\\aece5e58c4cf64f78c9e3bccc03bda00a1c56ee594e7081cc97810825cad01da\\\\session-3891b7ef-66b8-4a25-a922-5f7f56b0f910\\\\.weftmate-web-sources\\\\capture-f4a25885-90b3-4c30-a3ee-296c70ba6311.txt\"}"
