{
  "arguments": "{"description":"关键断言核对","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"Do not browse, write files or delegate. List each draft claim → source number + exact phrase → meaning/scope/numbers verdict. Challenge unsupported inferences even if the writer said they were verified. Runtime build rules do not prove addon build rules; a commit title can be intermediate/reverted; Node-API is an exception to ordinary module ABI mismatch. Return concise corrections or 未在官方资料中确认, not a rewritten article.\n\nContext: reviewing a Chinese document about RFC 9110 (HTTP Semantics) §15.4 redirection status codes 301/302/303/307/308, comparing permanence and request-method rewriting, especially whether POST must or may become GET on automatic redirect.\n\nNumbered exact source passages (all captured from official rfc-editor.org RFC 9110 pages):\n\n[1] capture E, URL https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-15.4 (redirected to https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html), capturedAt 2026-10-10T03:24:08.468Z. From the HTML table of contents: \"15.4.  Redirection 3xx\", \"15.4.2.  301 Moved Permanently\", \"15.4.3.  302 Found\", \"15.4.4.  303 See Other\", \"15.4.8.  307 Temporary Redirect\", \"15.4.9.  308 Permanent Redirect\".\n\n[2] capture E, same URL/time, line 2613: \"For 201 (Created) responses, the Location value refers to the primary resource created by the request. For 3xx (Redirection) responses, the Location value refers to the preferred target resource for automatically redirecting the request.\"\n\n[3] capture C, URL https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.txt, capturedAt 2026-10-10T03:20:51.504Z, §9.3.3 POST: \"If the result of processing a POST would be equivalent to a representation of an existing resource, an origin server MAY redirect the user agent to that resource by sending a 303 (See Other) response with the existing resource's identifier in the Location field.\"\n\n[4] capture 7a4f2878, URL https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html (about PUT method and redirects), capturedAt 2026-10-10T03:13:28.807Z: \"the user agent MAY then make its own decision regarding whether or not to redirect the request.\"\n\nDraft claims to check:\n\nC1. RFC 9110 §15.4 将 301/302/303/307/308 分为五个小节，小节标题分别标明 301 Moved Permanently、302 Found、303 See Other、307 Temporary Redirect、308 Permanent Redirect。[1]\n\nC2. 3xx 响应的 Location 值指向自动重定向请求时的首选目标资源。[2]\n\nC3. 对 POST 结果与既有资源表示等价的情形，源站 MAY 以 303 将用户代理重定向到该资源。[3]\n\nC4. 关于用户代理是否自动跟随重定向，RFC 9110 中有一处表述为 MAY 自行决定。[4]\n\nC5. 301、302、303、307、308 各自在 §15.4 中关于\"永久/临时\"的逐字定义句。—— writer marks this as 未在官方资料中确认 (only TOC headings were captured, no section body text).\n\nC6. 五个状态码各自对请求方法转换（method rewriting）的规则，特别是 301/302 对 POST 等方法的处理、303 对非 HEAD/GET 方法转换、307/308 要求方法不变的逐字规则。—— writer marks this as 未在官方资料中确认 (grep for method-rewriting sentences returned zero hits across all captures).\n\nC7. POST 自动重定向时\"可以(MAY)改成 GET\"或\"必须(MUST)改成 GET\"在 RFC 9110 中的逐字规定。—— writer marks this as 未在官方资料中确认 (no MUST/MAY method-conversion sentence was captured).\n\nVerdicts requested per claim: supported / unsupported inference / 未在官方资料中确认."}",
