          "text": "{\"snapshotId\":\"capture-e66d7863-4777-452e-a9a1-7a596cd43bef\",\"url\":\"https://react.dev/blog/2024/12/05/react-19\",\"title\":\"React v19 – React\",\"capturedAt\":\"2026-10-10T03:28:28.940Z\",\"text\":\"[characters 0-24]\\nBLOG\\nCopy page\\nReact v19\\n\\n[characters 26-61]\\nDecember 05, 2024 by The React Team\\n\\n[characters 63-92]\\nNote\\nReact 19 is now stable! \\n\\n[characters 94-172]\\nAdditions since this post was originally shared with the React 19 RC in April:\\n\\n[characters 174-290]\\nPre-warming for suspended trees: see Improvements to Suspense.\\nReact DOM static APIs: see New React DOM Static APIs.\\n\\n[characters 292-367]\\nThe date for this post has been updated to reflect the stable release date.\\n\\n[characters 369-403]\\nReact v19 is now available on npm!\\n\\n[characters 405-605]\\nIn our React 19 Upgrade Guide, we shared step-by-step instructions for upgrading your app to React 19. In this post, we’ll give an overview of the new features in React 19, and how you can adopt them.\\n\\n[characters 607-669]\\nWhat’s new in React 19\\nImprovements in React 19\\nHow to upgrade\\n\\n[characters 671-725]\\nFor a list of breaking changes, see the Upgrade Guide.\\n\\n[characters 727-759]\\nWhat’s new in React 19 \\nActions \\n\\n[characters 761-1095]\\nA common use case in React apps is to perform a data mutation and then update state in response. For example, when a user submits a form to change their name, you will make an API request, and then handle the response. In the past, you would need to handle pending states, errors, optimistic updates, and sequential requests manually.\\n\\n[characters 1097-1167]\\nFor example, you could handle the pending and error state in useState:\\n\\n[characters 1169-1186]\\n// Before Actions\\n\\n[characters 1188-1213]\\nfunction UpdateName({}) {\\n\\n[characters 1215-1254]\\n  const [name, setName] = useState(\\\"\\\");\\n\\n[characters 1256-1299]\\n  const [error, setError] = useState(null);\\n\\n[characters 1301-1353]\\n  const [isPending, setIsPending] = useState(false);\\n\\n[characters 1357-1393]\\n  const handleSubmit = async () => {\\n\\n[characters 1420-1461]\\n    const error = await updateName(name);\\n\\n[characters 1463-1487]\\n    setIsPending(false);\\n\\n[characters 1553-1575]\\n    redirect(\\\"/path\\\");\\n\\n[characters 1608-1686]\\n      <input value={name} onChange={(event) => setName(event.target.value)} />\\n\\n[characters 1688-1746]\\n      <button onClick={handleSubmit} disabled={isPending}>\\n\\n[characters 1748-1762]\\n        Update\\n\\n[characters 1835-1988]\\nIn React 19, we’re adding support for using async functions in transitions to handle pending states, errors, forms, and optimistic updates automatically.\\n\\n[characters 1990-2065]\\nFor example, you can use useTransition to handle the pending state for you:\\n\\n[characters 2067-2102]\\n// Using pending state from Actions\\n\\n[characters 2104-2129]\\nfunction UpdateName({}) {\\n\\n[characters 2131-2170]\\n  const [name, setName] = useState(\\\"\\\");\\n\\n[characters 2172-2215]\\n  const [error, setError] = useState(null);\\n\\n[characters 2217-2272]\\n  const [isPending, startTransition] = useTransition();\\n\\n[characters 2276-2306]\\n  const handleSubmit = () => {\\n\\n[characters 2308-2341]\\n    startTransition(async () => {\\n\\n[characters 2343-2386]\\n      const error = await updateName(name);\\n\\n[characters 2460-2484]\\n      redirect(\\\"/path\\\");\\n\\n[characters 2525-2603]\\n      <input value={name} onChange={(event) => setName(event.target.value)} />\\n\\n[characters 2605-2663]\\n      <button onClick={handleSubmit} disabled={isPending}>\\n\\n[characters 2665-2679]\\n        Update\\n\\n[characters 2752-2996]\\nThe async transition will immediately set the isPending state to true, make the async request(s), and switch isPending to false after any transitions. This allows you to keep the current UI responsive and interactive while the data is changing.\\n\\n[characters 2998-3077]\\nNote\\nBy convention, functions that use async transitions are called “Actions”. \\n\\n[characters 3079-3132]\\nActions automatically manage submitting data for you:\\n\\n[characters 3134-3801]\\nPending state: Actions provide a pending state tha\n\n[... tool result middle pruned ...]\n\n245,\"text\":\"function ChangeName({ name, setName }) {\"},{\"charStart\":4247,\"charEnd\":4305,\"text\":\"  const [error, submitAction, isPending] = useActionState(\"},{\"charStart\":4307,\"charEnd\":4347,\"text\":\"    async (previousState, formData) => {\"},{\"charStart\":4349,\"charEnd\":4408,\"text\":\"      const error = await updateName(formData.get(\\\"name\\\"));\"},{\"charStart\":4462,\"charEnd\":4486,\"text\":\"      redirect(\\\"/path\\\");\"},{\"charStart\":4547,\"charEnd\":4579,\"text\":\"    <form action={submitAction}>\"},{\"charStart\":4581,\"charEnd\":4620,\"text\":\"      <input type=\\\"text\\\" name=\\\"name\\\" />\"},{\"charStart\":4622,\"charEnd\":4686,\"text\":\"      <button type=\\\"submit\\\" disabled={isPending}>Update</button>\"},{\"charStart\":4743,\"charEnd\":4747,\"text\":\"In t\"}],\"sourcePath\":\"C:\\\\Temp\\\\weftmate-fact1-d4639fa5-93d3-4c19-b0c5-3adfc5860d9e\\\\profile\\\\conversations\\\\aece5e58c4cf64f78c9e3bccc03bda00a1c56ee594e7081cc97810825cad01da\\\\session-9c89e02e-6ffd-41df-b71a-2369a1cb8e06\\\\.weftmate-web-sources\\\\capture-e66d7863-4777-452e-a9a1-7a596cd43bef.txt\"}"
